{title: Changes In Latitude}
{artist: Jimmy Buffet}
{key: D}
{tempo: 126}
{duration: 3:45}

{start_of_part: Intro}
[G][D][A][D]
[G][D][A][G]
[D]
{end_of_part}


{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I took off for a week[G]end last month
Just to [A]try and recall the whole [D]year
All of the faces and all[G] of the places
Won[A]derin' where they all disap[D]peared
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_part: Pre-Chorus}
[Bm]I didn't ponder the ques[F#m]tion too long
I was [G]hungry and went out for a [A]bite
Ran [G]into a chum with a [D]bottle of rum
And we [A]wound up drinkin' all [D]night
{end_of_part}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It's those [G]changes in latitudes, [D]changes in attitudes
[A]Nothing remains quite the [D]same
With [G]all of our running and all[D] of our cunning
If [A]we couldn't laugh, we would all[G] go in[D]sane
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Reading departure signs [G]in some big airport
Re[A]minds me of the places I've [D]been
Visions of good times that [G]brought so much pleasure
Makes me[A] want to go back a[D]gain
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_part: Pre-Chorus}
If it [Bm]suddenly ended tomor[F#m]row
I could [G]somehow adjust to the [A]fall
[G]Good times and riches and [D]son of a bitches
I've [A]seen more than I can re[D]call
{end_of_part}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
These [G]changes in latitudes, [D]changes in attitudes
[A]Nothing remains quite the [D]same
Through [G]all of the islands and all[D] of the highlands
If [A]we couldn't laugh we would all[G] go in[D]sane
{end_of_chorus}


{start_of_part: Solo}
[G][D][A][G]
{end_of_part}


{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[D]
{end_of_bridge}


{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I [D]think about Paris when I'm[G] high on red wine
I [A]wish I could jump on a [D]plane
And so many nights I just [G]dream of the ocean
God, I [A]wish she was sailin' a[D]gain
{end_of_verse}


{start_of_part: Pre-Chorus}
Oh, [Bm]yesterdays are over my shoul[F#m]der
So I[G] can't look back for too [A]long
There's just [G]too much to see waiting in[D] front of me
And I [A]know that I just can't go [D]wrong
{end_of_part}


{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With these [G]changes in latitudes, [D]changes in attitudes
[A]Nothing remains quite the [D]same
With [G]all of my running and all[D] of my cunning
If I[A] couldn't laugh I just [G]would go in[D]sane
{end_of_chorus}


{comment: Post-Chorus}
[A]If we couldn't laugh we just would[G] go in[D]sane
[A]If we weren't all crazy we [G]would [A]go in[G]sane


{start_of_part: Outro}
